## Forms in this project
Forms are written with the form helpers from 'sygnal' in the component's own state, intent and model (this project doesn't use the `form` behavior), with a zod schema (zod is installed): `formErrors(schema, values)` gives the errors by field name (`{}` when valid), `checkForm(schema, values).value` the schema's output, `setField(values, name, value)` new values, `replyErrors(reply, values)` server errors by field name, `focusInvalid(errors, '.signup')` an ELEMENT command that focuses the first invalid field, and `processForm(DOM.select('.signup'))` every named field's value on input and submit:
```jsx
function Signup({ state, uid }) {
  const error = state.touched.email || state.submitted ? formErrors(signupSchema, state.values).email : ''
  return (
    <form className="signup" noValidate>
      <label for={uid('email')}>Email</label>
      <input id={uid('email')} name="email" value={state.values.email} aria-invalid={String(!!error)} aria-describedby={uid('email-error')} />
      <p id={uid('email-error')}>{error}</p>
      <button type="submit">Sign up</button>
    </form>
  )
}
Signup.initialState = { values: { email: '' }, touched: {}, submitted: false }
Signup.intent = ({ DOM }) => ({
  CHANGE: DOM.select('.signup').events('input').map((e) => ({ name: e.target.name, value: e.target.value })),
  BLUR: DOM.select('.signup').events('focusout').map((e) => e.target.name),
  SUBMIT: DOM.select('.signup').events('submit', { preventDefault: true }),
})
Signup.model = {
  CHANGE: (state, { name, value }) => ({ ...state, values: setField(state.values, name, value) }),
  BLUR: (state, name) => ({ ...state, touched: { ...state.touched, [name]: true } }),
  SUBMIT: {
    STATE: (state) => ({ ...state, submitted: true }),
    ELEMENT: (state) => focusInvalid(formErrors(signupSchema, state.values), '.signup'),
    HTTP: (state) => (Object.keys(formErrors(signupSchema, state.values)).length ? ABORT
      : { url: '/api/signup', method: 'POST', json: checkForm(signupSchema, state.values).value, ok: 'SIGNED_UP', error: 'REFUSED' }),
  },
}
// main.js: run(App, { HTTP: makeFetchDriver() })
```
- Field arrays: rows with an `id` in `values`, named `items.<id>.field` (`setField` and `formErrors` address rows by id), rendered with a Collection whose items send add/remove to the parent.
- Server errors: keep `replyErrors(reply, state.values)` in state, show them at once, and send `focusInvalid` with them.
